\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Overview of the MAGNet{} architecture. The input molecular graph is processed by a multi-scale GNN to extract features at different topological depths (1-hop, 2-hop, 3-hop). The cross-scale attention mechanism fuses these features using learned gating and multi-head attention. The attention pooling module produces a fixed-size graph-level representation using learnable query vectors. Finally, an MLP classifier head produces the property prediction.}}{4}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:architecture}{{1}{4}{Overview of the \modelname {} architecture. The input molecular graph is processed by a multi-scale GNN to extract features at different topological depths (1-hop, 2-hop, 3-hop). The cross-scale attention mechanism fuses these features using learned gating and multi-head attention. The attention pooling module produces a fixed-size graph-level representation using learnable query vectors. Finally, an MLP classifier head produces the property prediction}{figure.1}{}}
